
@startuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Student {
    - studentId : String
    - name : String
    - email : String
    --
    + viewAvailability() : void
    + bookRoom(room : Room, start : DateTime, end : DateTime) : Booking
    + cancelBooking(booking : Booking) : void
}

class Administrator {
    - administratorId : String
    - name : String
    - email : String
    --
    + blockRoom(room : Room) : void
    + unblockRoom(room : Room) : void
    + reviewRoomUsage(start : DateTime, end : DateTime) : void
}

class Room {
    - roomId : String
    - name : String
    - blocked : Boolean
    --
    + isAvailable(start : DateTime, end : DateTime) : Boolean
    + block() : void
    + unblock() : void
}

class Booking {
    - bookingId : String
    - startTime : DateTime
    - endTime : DateTime
    - status : String
    --
    + cancel() : void
    + isValid() : Boolean
}

Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes
Room "1" -- "0..*" Booking : is reserved by

Administrator ..> Room : manages
Administrator ..> Booking : reviews usage

Booking --> Room : reserves
Booking --> Student : belongs to

note right of Booking
Constraints:
R1: booking starts in the future
R2: duration <= 2 hours
R3: bookings for the same room
    must not overlap
R4: blocked rooms cannot be booked
end note

note bottom
Assumptions:
1. Each Booking belongs to exactly one Student.
2. Each Booking reserves exactly one Room.
3. A Student may have zero or more bookings.
4. A Room may have zero or more bookings over time.
5. Administrator is a domain role, but no inheritance
   hierarchy is assumed.
6. Confirmation is treated as system behavior from UC-04;
   no separate Confirmation class is required.
7. Authentication, payment, database, equipment and
   notification infrastructure are outside the domain model.
end note

@enduml

